# Two tasks that own the same path, either of which could be claimed while the
# other is in flight. That is the collision the ownership rule exists to make
# impossible, and it is refused where a human eye used to catch it.
run available
exit 3
file tasks/M1-01.md
	---
	id: M1-01
	owns:
	  - crates/normalize
	depends_on: []
	exclusive: no
	---
file tasks/M1-02.md
	---
	id: M1-02
	owns:
	  - crates/normalize
	depends_on: []
	exclusive: no
	---
stderr
	tasks.sh: tasks/M1-02.md: owns crates/normalize, which overlaps the crates/normalize that M1-01 owns, and neither depends on the other
